## LoL Patch 26.21 Tier List: the best champions for every role

Which champions are worth playing in League of Legends Patch 26.21? This update brings significant changes across several roles, including buffs for Sion, Taliyah, Nunu and Zyra, as well as nerfs affecting popular picks such as Lee Sin, Rammus, Jinx and Tristana.

This tier list covers Top, Jungle, Mid, ADC and Support, with explanations of the balance changes that may influence the meta. The recommendations combine Riot's official patch notes with the first available ranked data.

**Important:** the patch has only just launched, so these rankings are provisional. Early results may vary by rank, region and sample size. Champion placements should be reviewed as more role-specific matches become available.

## Patch 26.21 tier list overview

| Role | Recommended picks | What to watch |
|---|---|---|
| Top | Sion, Darius, Volibear, Garen | Sion and Darius receive favorable changes; Yone loses some damage. |
| Jungle | Taliyah, Shyvana, Wukong, Nunu & Willump | Taliyah and Nunu are buffed; Rammus, Lee Sin and Nidalee are toned down. |
| Mid | Orianna, Ryze, Fizz, Gwen | Orianna and Ryze gain scaling; Qiyana and Viktor are nerfed. |
| ADC | Miss Fortune, Kog'Maw, Jinx, Caitlyn | Miss Fortune receives compensation buffs; Jinx and Caitlyn lose some power. |
| Support | Zyra, Vel'Koz, Taric, Leona | Zyra and Vel'Koz are buffed; Taric remains a utility-focused option. |

This is a **provisional editorial tier list**, not a definitive statistical ranking of every champion. Recommendations should be refined using data for each role, rank and region.

## Top: best champions in Patch 26.21

### Sion — Provisional A tier

Sion gains more health per level, increasing from 87 to 95, and receives an improvement to the bonus damage on his ultimate when charging it. These changes may help him become more consistent in longer games.

**Why play him:** he offers durability, engage and the ability to create space in teamfights.

**Best for:** players who prefer durable champions and want to contribute to teamfights without relying entirely on winning lane.

### Darius — Provisional A tier

Darius's Q cooldown at the final rank decreases from 5 to 4 seconds. This is a meaningful improvement for extended trades, although it does not guarantee a higher overall win rate.

**Why play him:** he can punish lane mistakes and become a major threat in prolonged fights.

**Best for:** aggressive players who understand melee matchups.

### Volibear — Provisional A tier

Volibear remains an interesting option for players who want dueling power, durability and lane pressure. He did not receive a major direct change in this patch, so his placement depends more on statistical performance than on the patch notes.

### Garen — Provisional A tier

Garen is an accessible alternative for players looking for consistency and a straightforward game plan. This is an editorial recommendation, not a claim that he received a direct buff in Patch 26.21.

**Top lane watchlist:** Yone loses some damage on Q, while Varus's adjustments also affect his top-lane variant. Both picks should be reevaluated using Top-specific statistics before assigning a definitive tier.

## Jungle: best champions in Patch 26.21

### Taliyah — Provisional A tier, with upward potential

Taliyah receives more damage on E, including its detonation. The ability also deals 225% damage to monsters.

**Why play her:** she can use crowd control and damage to clear camps and create gank opportunities.

**Best for:** players who enjoy mage junglers, zone control and map rotations.

### Shyvana — Provisional A tier

Shyvana appears among the champions with solid results in the available version data. Her recommendation is based on observed performance rather than a direct buff in this patch.

**Why play her:** she combines camp clearing, scaling and sustained damage.

### Wukong — Provisional A tier

Wukong receives compensation through increased health regeneration but loses some early passive armor per stack.

**Why play him:** he offers engage and substantial impact in teamfights.

**What to watch:** the balance between his jungle performance and his lane presence may shift following these changes.

### Nunu & Willump — Provisional A tier

The maximum damage on Nunu's ultimate increases at all ranks, from 625/925/1275 to 750/1100/1450, while its AP scaling remains unchanged.

**Why play them:** they can punish grouped enemies and exploit poor positioning.

**Jungle watchlist:** Rammus loses some defensive scaling on W. Lee Sin receives a longer W cooldown and lower ultimate damage. Nidalee also loses W damage and E attack speed. These nerfs reduce some of their power but do not automatically make them uncompetitive.

## Mid: best champions in Patch 26.21

### Orianna — Provisional A tier

Orianna gains better AP ratios on Q and W, increasing her damage potential later in the game.

**Why play her:** she offers wave control, utility and an ultimate that can decide teamfights.

**Best for:** players who prefer control mages and coordinated team play.

### Ryze — Provisional A tier

Ryze receives improvements to Q scaling, movement speed and W damage. These changes are intended to reward players who reach the later stages of the game.

**Why play him:** he combines sustained damage, mobility and map pressure.

**Best for:** players willing to invest time in mastering his combos and wave management.

### Fizz — Provisional A tier

Fizz appears among the champions with competitive results in the available patch data. He did not receive a direct buff in this update.

**Why play him:** he can punish poor positioning and eliminate priority targets.

**Best for:** players who enjoy assassins and creating advantages through roaming and kills.

### Gwen — Provisional A tier

The available early data shows competitive results for Gwen in Mid, although her sample size and pick rate should be considered before treating those results as universally representative.

**Why play her:** she can provide sustained damage and perform well in extended fights.

**Mid watchlist:** Qiyana receives a Q damage reduction, while Viktor loses movement speed and part of his Q shield. Azir, meanwhile, gains mana growth. These changes may alter matchups, but their final impact needs to be confirmed with more games.

## ADC: best champions in Patch 26.21

### Miss Fortune — Provisional A tier, with upward potential

Miss Fortune receives more E damage and increased ultimate damage. These changes partly compensate for the loss of power associated with the Hubris adjustment.

**Why play her:** she can apply lane pressure and deal substantial damage when enemies group together.

**Best for:** players who prefer a marksman with a clear laning plan and a teamfight-changing ultimate.

### Kog'Maw — Provisional A tier

Kog'Maw appears among the champions with strong results in the available version data, although he did not receive a major direct change in Patch 26.21.

**Why play him:** he provides sustained damage and can shred durable targets when given enough time and protection.

**Best for:** players who prefer scaling and careful positioning in fights.

### Jinx — Provisional A tier

Jinx loses attack damage per level and base health, with the goal of reducing her dominance in the meta.

**Why keep considering her:** she retains her scaling-carry identity and can take over fights through resets.

**What to watch:** her popularity and performance following the nerf. There is no need to discard her automatically.

### Caitlyn — Provisional A tier

Caitlyn loses some passive damage scaling but gains more base damage on Q. The change shifts some of her power from late game toward the laning phase.

**Why play her:** she can use her range and lane pressure to create early advantages.

**ADC watchlist:** Tristana loses attack speed on the early ranks of Q. Varus receives a redistribution of power between Q and W, intended to limit his Top variant and allow more targeted tuning for Bot. Post-patch statistics will determine whether these champions maintain their positions.

## Support: best champions in Patch 26.21

### Zyra — Provisional A tier, with upward potential

Zyra receives a lower seed-ammunition cooldown on W at several ranks. Early data from ggez.gg recorded a 5.9 percentage-point increase in win rate, although this is an initial all-rank sample rather than a guarantee of future performance.

**Why play her:** she can control zones, pressure lanes with plants and punish poor positioning.

**Best for:** players who prefer damage-oriented supports and area control.

### Vel'Koz — Provisional A tier, with upward potential

Vel'Koz gains passive damage, increasing from 35–180 (+60% AP) to 35–205 (+65% AP).

**Why play him:** he rewards accurate ability combos and can pressure enemies from range.

**Best for:** players who prefer long-range poke and magic damage.

### Taric — Provisional A tier

Taric receives behavior improvements when casting abilities on a linked ally who becomes untargetable during the cast. This makes some interactions more reliable.

**Why play him:** he offers protection, healing and utility in coordinated fights.

### Leona — Provisional A tier

Leona remains an option for players who want engage and crowd control. Her inclusion is editorial and does not imply a direct buff in this patch.

**Support watchlist:** Zyra and Vel'Koz may increase interest in damage-oriented supports, while Taric remains an alternative focused on protection. Final placements should be based on Support-specific data and matchups.

